      "math_academy_id": "q-183325",
      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "Describe the set $S=\\{5,6,7,...,50\\}$ using a conditional definition.\n\n$$\nS=\\{x\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,{{field-2}}\\le x\\le {{field-3}}\\}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The set $S$ contains all natural numbers between $5$ and $50$ (including $5$ and $50$).\n\nTherefore, the set can be written as\n\n$$\nS=\\{x\\in N\\,:\\,5\\le x\\le 50\\}.\n$$\n\n**Note**: This definition is not unique. For example:\n\n- We can write $x\\in Z.$ This gives\n\n$$\nS=\\{x\\in Z\\,:\\,5\\le x\\le 50\\}.\n$$\n\n- We can write $4<x<51.$ This gives\n\n$$\nS=\\{x\\in N\\,:\\,4<x<51\\},\n$$\n\nor, writing $x\\in Z$ as before, we have\n\n$$\nS=\\{x\\in Z\\,:\\,4<x<51\\}.\n$$",
